<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Margarita Island</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Margarita Island is the largest island of Venezuela, in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a> north-east of the mainland, and with nearby islands forms the state of Nueva Esparta. Sighted by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus">Columbus</a> in 1498, it was valued for its pearl fisheries in the 16th century. It was an early patriot stronghold in the war of independence, and Bolívar's expedition landed there in 1816.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/margarita-island.jpg" alt="Margarita Island" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: No machine-readable author provided. DennisITA assumed (based on copyright claims). · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PlayaElAgua_(Margarita-VEN).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
